	<h1 class="page-title">Consulting &amp; assignments</h1>
	<p class="page-lede">Energy policy, power sector governance and international cooperation — in France and internationally.</p>
	<div class="page-body ip-split">
<section class="ip-sec ip-sec--intro">
<div class="ip-sec-body">
<p>I work with institutions, operators, local governments and consultancies on energy policy, power sector governance and international cooperation. Short and medium-length assignments, in France and internationally, with one simple principle: the work starts from the client's files, not from a catalogue.</p>

<p>Assignments are carried by <strong>Lapin Bleu SASU</strong> (Lyon), a mission-driven company (<em>société à mission</em>) and registered training provider (NDA 84692485869): invoicing in France and internationally, a structure suited to public and institutional procurement.</p>
</div>
</section>

<section class="ip-sec">
<h2>Types of assignments</h2>
<div class="ip-sec-body">
<div class="ip-cards ip-cards--2">
<div class="hp-feature ip-card">
	<h3>Sector diagnostics and framing notes</h3>
	<p>Electricity markets and grids, regulation, concessions, sector reforms. Institutional interviews, documentary and regulatory analysis, international comparisons, organisational recommendations.</p>
	<div class="ip-card-foot">
		<span class="hp-feature-kind">Example deliverables:</span> sector framing note, multi-criteria comparative analysis, regulatory mapping, organisational recommendations for a regulator or ministry.
	</div>
</div>

<div class="hp-feature ip-card">
	<h3>Capacity building and training design</h3>
	<p>Catalogues, career-track curricula and modules for executives, elected officials and staff, from initial diagnosis to delivery.</p>
	<div class="ip-card-foot">
		<span class="hp-feature-kind">Recent example:</span> a full training catalogue of 23 modules and 6 career tracks designed for a public agency in a Central African state, within a reform programme financed by a multilateral donor (see case study below).
	</div>
</div>

<div class="hp-feature ip-card">
	<h3>Stakeholder engagement and social acceptability</h3>
	<p>Dialogue with users and local authorities, tariff pedagogy, stakeholder mapping. Acceptability is treated as a risk factor on reform outcomes, not as a communications issue.</p>
	<div class="ip-card-foot">
		<span class="hp-feature-kind">Typical contexts:</span> tariff increase after a prolonged freeze, smart meter roll-out, energy infrastructure siting, restructuring of public utilities.
	</div>
</div>

<div class="hp-feature ip-card">
	<h3>Institutional and crisis communications</h3>
	<p>Sensitive files, environmental controversies, relations with elected officials, administrations and the media.</p>
	<div class="ip-card-foot">
		<span class="hp-feature-kind">Experience:</span> 12 years in local government handling public communications, crisis management and institutional relations.
	</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</section>

<section class="ip-sec">
<h2>Case study: power sector reform in a Central African state (2026)</h2>
<div class="ip-sec-body">
<p>Independent field mission conducted in 2026 in the capital of a Central African state, within the environment of a power sector reform programme financed by a multilateral donor (a <em>Program-for-Results</em> operation).</p>

<ul class="ip-list">
<li><strong>Institutional interviews</strong> across the sector: the programme's coordination unit (ministry in charge of energy), the national rural electrification agency, a bilateral donor present in-country.</li>
<li><strong>Deliverables handed</strong> to the programme coordinator: a vision note proposing to develop a national institution into a regional school for Central Africa's electricity workforce; a training catalogue (23 modules, 6 career tracks, 1 regional capstone project); a technical support proposal.</li>
<li><strong>Results-linked design:</strong> documents designed to serve the results indicators of a <em>Program-for-Results</em> operation (disbursement tied to results, not expenditure) and the regional integration agenda of the regional power pool.</li>
<li><strong>Acceptability module:</strong> securing reform outcomes — user acceptability, tariff pedagogy after a prolonged freeze, smart meter roll-out, engagement with users and local authorities.</li>
</ul>
</div>
</section>

<section class="ip-sec">
<h2>Methods</h2>
<div class="ip-sec-body">
<p>Semi-structured institutional interviews, documentary and regulatory analysis, comparative case studies, multi-criteria international benchmarking, stakeholder mapping, training design. Written and oral deliverables in French and English.</p>
</div>
</section>

